    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This study examines the expansion of Vocational Education and Training (VET) in Brazil’s secondary school system after the enactment of the 2017 high school reform. Employing a qualitative case study methodology across three states, it examines how state capacity, political conditions, and the professionals’ agency influence VET policy implementation. Through in-depth interviews and document analysis, the study uncovers the complexities of integrating VET into secondary education. Findings indicate that subnational context is crucial, with ideological and capacity differences driving variations. States are adopting experimental approaches to address resource constraints, while education professionals have limited but notable agency, which is shaped by decision-making processes and working conditions. Despite heavy reliance on on-the-ground actors, the policy lacks adequate support, leading to challenges that reinforce negative perceptions of VET as a viable educational path. This study contributes to understanding the implementation of education reform and the complexities of integrating vocational and academic schooling.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Hortencio, M. (2024). From Policy to Practice: Investigating the Implementation of Vocational Education in Brazil’s Secondary Schools. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/db439yz6237. https://doi.org/10.25740/db439yz6237.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
